<article class="env-lemma" id="04VH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04VH">Lemma <span data-tag="04VH">4.27.11</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category and let $S$ be a right multiplicative system. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The relation on pairs defined above is an equivalence relation. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The composition rule given above is well defined on equivalence classes. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Composition is associative (and the identity morphisms satisfy the identity axioms), and hence $S^{-1}\mathcal{C}$ is a category. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma is dual to Lemma <a href="/tag/04VD" data-tag="04VD">4.27.2</a>. It follows formally from that lemma by replacing $\mathcal{C}$ by its opposite category in which $S$ is a left multiplicative system. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>